window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-e5103cdd8f14fbfa"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"refresh-course-materials\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">更新课程材料</h1> <p>把整门课程作为一个相互关联的系统来审阅。</p> <p>使用 Google Drive 和文档工具，让 ChatGPT 审阅教学大纲、演示文稿、阅读材料、作业、评分量规和课程成果，然后生成有证据支持的课程更新计划；不直接修改源文件。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>正在为新学期做准备的教师。</li> <li>课程材料分散在多份文件、多个格式中且逐渐发生变化的课程。</li> <li>需要先有证据、经教师批准后才能修改源文件的审阅工作。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>google-drive</code></td> <td>收集教学大纲、演示文稿、阅读材料、作业、评分量规和以往课程笔记。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$documents</code></td> <td>生成结构清晰、便于审阅的课程更新计划。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>制定课程更新计划</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请审阅我提供的教学大纲、讲课演示文稿、阅读清单、作业、评分量规、课程成果、以往课程笔记和学期日历。\n\n请找出：\n- 已过时的示例或阅读材料\n- 重复内容\n- 课程成果与考核之间的对应缺口\n- 给学生的指导不一致之处\n- 工作量异常集中的周次\n\n请制定优先级明确的课程更新计划，并为每项建议提供证据。修改任何源文件之前先停下来供我审阅。\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">插件</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"review-the-course-as-a-system\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">将课程作为一个整体来审阅</h2> <p>如果能把教学大纲、课程成果、课程内容、阅读材料、作业和评分量规放在一起审阅，课程更新会更有效。运行起始提示词前，请收集当前源文件，并说明哪些文件是权威版本。</p> <p>同时提供学期日历和以往课程笔记，帮助 ChatGPT 区分有意安排的教学顺序和文件之间逐渐出现的偏差。</p> <p><a id=\"build-the-refresh-plan\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">制定更新计划</h2> <p>请 ChatGPT：</p> <ol> <li>将学习成果对应到课程内容和考核方式。</li> <li>根据来源证据标记过时、重复或不一致的材料。</li> <li>找出工作量高峰以及对学生不够清楚的指导。</li> <li>按学生影响、所需投入和依赖关系排列修改优先级。</li> <li>将建议与需要教师判断的问题分开。</li> </ol> <p>第一步应当先产出计划，而不是直接重写课程文件。</p> <p><a id=\"review-before-revising\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">修改前先审阅</h2> <p>对照所引用的来源检查每项建议。确认必修内容、无障碍指导、机构政策和教师裁量权都得到准确体现。</p> <p>计划获批后，可以在同一聊天中继续分批修改文件。保留原件，并在每轮修改后要求提供变更摘要。</p>","en":"<h1 id=\"refresh-course-materials\">Refresh course materials</h1> <p>Review a course as one connected system.</p> <p>Use ChatGPT with Google Drive and document tools to review syllabi, slides, readings, assignments, rubrics, and outcomes, then return an evidence-backed course refresh plan without changing source files.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Faculty preparing a course for a new term.</li> <li>Courses whose materials have evolved across several files and formats.</li> <li>Reviews that need evidence and faculty approval before source files change.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>google-drive</code></td> <td>Gather the syllabus, slides, readings, assignments, rubrics, and prior course notes.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>$documents</code></td> <td>Produce a structured, review-ready course refresh plan.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Build a Course Refresh Plan</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Review the syllabus, lecture slides, reading list, assignments, rubrics, course outcomes, prior course notes, and term calendar I provide.\n\nIdentify:\n- outdated examples or readings\n- duplicated content\n- alignment gaps between outcomes and assessments\n- inconsistent student guidance\n- weeks with unusually heavy workload\n\nCreate a prioritized course refresh plan with evidence for every recommendation. Stop for my review before revising any source files.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dea5d8982f047a3a\">Plugins</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"review-the-course-as-a-system\">Review the course as a system</h2> <p>A course refresh works best when the syllabus, outcomes, lessons, readings, assignments, and rubrics are reviewed together. Gather the current source files and identify which documents are authoritative before you run the starter prompt.</p> <p>Include the term calendar and prior course notes so ChatGPT can distinguish intentional sequencing from drift between files.</p> <h2 id=\"build-the-refresh-plan\">Build the refresh plan</h2> <p>Ask ChatGPT to:</p> <ol> <li>Map learning outcomes to lessons and assessments.</li> <li>Flag outdated, duplicated, or inconsistent material with source evidence.</li> <li>Identify workload spikes and unclear student guidance.</li> <li>Rank revisions by student impact, effort, and dependency.</li> <li>Separate proposed changes from questions that require faculty judgment.</li> </ol> <p>The first output should be a plan, not rewritten course files.</p> <h2 id=\"review-before-revising\">Review before revising</h2> <p>Check every recommendation against the cited source. Confirm that required content, accessibility guidance, institutional policy, and instructor discretion are represented correctly.</p> <p>After approving the plan, continue in the same chat and revise one group of files at a time. Preserve the originals and ask for a change summary after each revision pass.</p>"};
